{
  "reason": "Open items (2026-11-19), reviewed case by case against the diff of every output (rules, engine and evidence for AL, DE and NH, MD and DO). (1) DE: the 2 hour controlled substance CE is attested at each CSR renewal (24 Del. Admin. Code Uniform Controlled Substances Act Regs. 3.1; registrations expire June 30 of odd years), so the topic carries period {registration: \"csr\"} and is counted over the 2 years ending at the physician's CSR expiration, or the state's next fixed one (2027-06-30 at the frozen date). Its note no longer says the app counts it in the license window; periodLabel names the CSR period; evidence names the period controlled_substance_registration_period. Both DE topics and the AL controlled substance topic (ACSC holders) carry csrHolders: true, so they drop out for a physician who said they do not prescribe there; evidence names appliesTo. No met value moves in these cases. (2) NH: Med 402.01(g) and (i) read on gc.nh.gov 2026-11-19. The board certification text names any American Specialty Board exam (initial or recertification) and current MOC, not ABMS alone; source and sourceUrl move from the Cornell mirror to the official gc.nh.gov rules page; the pain management topic cites RSA 318-B:41, VI and Med 402.01(o) and says it is still owed; verified 2026-11. Nothing else in these outputs changes.",
